<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="Solar-Cm-Theme" spTempo="205">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1954
Composer:	Miles Davis
Lyricist:	None — instrumental
Form:	12-bar blues
Style:	Modern jazz
Key:	C minor

“Solar” was first recorded by Miles Davis in 1954
and was copyrighted in his name in 1963. Its authorship
is disputed: evidence revealed in 2012 indicates that guitarist
Chuck Wayne recorded a nearly identical composition titled
“Sonny” in 1946, making Wayne a strong candidate for the original
composer, although Davis remains the official and customary credit.</spComments>
